<p>PwC Kenya's <em>Real Estate Outlook 2026</em> identifies three macro forces shaping the investment environment: a declining interest rate trajectory following CBK's policy normalisation cycle; a structural housing deficit estimated at 500,000 units annually by KNBS; and accelerating urbanisation at 4.0% per annum—more than double the global average of 1.8%—that continuously generates new demand for both residential and commercial real estate across Kenya's urban hierarchy.</p>
